# joetoo-kwin — curated source-transfer MANIFEST (Step 1.9)
#
# Used by tools/joetoo-kwin-stage-upstream, located in the joetoo-ai
# project root.  Reviewed and transferred into the joetoo-upstream source
# directory as a provenance record; tarup archives it as ordinary text.
#
# File format: GROUP|PROJECT_RELATIVE_SOURCE[|UPSTREAM_RELATIVE_TARGET]
#   GROUP: display-only announce/act/report label; does NOT select a folder.
#   SOURCE: one regular file beneath the joetoo-ai project root.
#   TARGET: optional basename/path relative to the curated upstream root.
#   Omitted TARGET means identical source and target path.
# Entries may be reordered for human readability; transfers follow file order.
# Put a companion README immediately after the configuration it documents.
# No directory is inferred from GROUP; SOURCE and optional TARGET control paths.
# Blank lines and whole-line comments beginning with # are ignored.
# No wildcard expansion, symlink dereferencing, traversal, or deletion.
# Each target path may appear only once. Add new inputs deliberately.
#
# Missing entries fail individually: author future documentation BEFORE
# considering --release-check to have passed; --apply can still stage
# existing files incrementally, with a nonzero final status for omissions.
#
# Configuration companion READMEs reside beside their relevant source
# config/example/module. The release README is a separately mapped root file.
# All are ordinary required entries in this one manifest (no glob).

